    "summary": "Scorching Dark Star, tight Hard To Handle, vibrant second‑set jams",
    "blurb": "The show bursts to life with a soaring Dark Star and a punchy Hard To Handle. Garcia’s lead is electric, Pigpen’s organ adds grit, and the band rides a wave of high‑energy improvisation through The Other One and Attics Of My Life.",
    "review": "On May 24 1970 the Dead made their UK debut in Newcastle‑Under‑Lyme, delivering a performance that still feels fresh decades later. After an uneven opening – the board mix is thin for the first few minutes – the band quickly finds its stride, launching into a blistering Dark Star that showcases Garcia’s scorching solos and Phil’s rolling bass foundation. The second set is a masterclass in pacing: Hard To Handle drives the tempo forward while the China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider sequence glows with Pigpen’s raw organ power. Highlights like The Other One, Attics Of My Life into Good Lovin’, and a crisp Cold Rain And Snow close out an evening of tight interplay between Mickey, Billy and the rest of the crew. With excellent soundboard clarity on the recommended recording, this historic show captures the Dead at a pivotal moment – energetic, adventurous, and unmistakably legendary.",
